# Opportunistic refactor (mandatory)

When you **touch** code in this repo, you **must** leave the area cleaner than you found it. Refactoring is not optional follow-up work.

## Trigger

Any task that edits a file also owns **one incremental extraction or dedup** in that same change set when the opportunity exists.

Opportunity exists when any of these apply:

- Pure logic duplicated inline or already living in a sibling module
- Constants duplicated instead of imported from a shared module
- URL builders, geo/math, sim clamps, or data normalizers still embedded in a large boot file
- A function has no closure over live UI/map state and can move out with explicit parameters

## Safe split axes (in order)

1. **Pure leaves** — `geo.js`, `api/urls.js`, `stores/simulation.js`, `viewshed-raster.js`, `constants.js`
2. **Map helpers** — pass `map`, `mapReady`, thresholds as args (`map-viewport.js`)
3. **Static config** — basemap tiles, layer IDs (`basemap.js`, `constants.js`)
4. **Data models** — sidebar normalization, cache helpers (`land-model.js`)
5. **Stateful domains** — only when actively rewriting that feature; use explicit factories, never mechanical closure splits

## Map UI (`assets/static/project-map/`)

- **`boot.js` orchestrates** Vue stores + domain app. **`domains/app.js`** is wiring only. New code goes in `stores/`, `map/`, `api/`, or `domains/*.js`.
- **Vue panels** (`panels/`) own sidebar list rendering — no manual `innerHTML` sync fan-out for sites.
- **Import shared modules**; do not copy const blocks or helper bodies back inline.
- After adding a module, update **MEMORY.md** § Workspace layout in the same change set.
- **Debug**: JS/CSS edits hot-serve from disk; **release**: `cargo build -p peaky` (rust-embed).

## Rust / other crates

Same rule: extract pure helpers to the nearest crate module when you edit a file >~300 lines or duplicate logic you can name in one line.

## Scope discipline

- **One extraction per touch** is enough. Do not expand into unrelated domains.
- **Do not** block a bugfix on a large rewrite. Ship the fix plus the smallest safe extraction.
- **Do not** split stateful domains speculatively (see failed partial ESM split). Factories only when the feature is in scope.

## Commits

- Refactor bundled with the feature → one commit is fine when inseparable.
- Refactor-only session → `refactor(<scope>): …` per commit-style rule.
- Never leave "TODO: extract later" without filing the extraction in MEMORY or doing it now.

## Self-check before done

- Did I touch `domains/app.js` without moving at least one pure helper out?
- Did I duplicate constants or URLs that belong in `constants.js` / `api/urls.js`?
- Is MEMORY.md updated if module layout changed?
